  "issue_number": 3408,
  "issue_title": "FE: wire Download CSV into the Surfaces and Endpoints table pages",
  "issue_body": "## Context\n`apps/ui/src/routes/surfaces.tsx` (`SurfacesPage`/`SurfacesTable`) and `apps/ui/src/routes/endpoints.tsx` (`EndpointsPage`/`EndpointsTable`) render their tables with no export affordance \u2014 a user browsing either page has no way to get the rows out as a file. Both backends already support it: `GET /api/v1/surfaces` is wrapped in `csvListQuery(\"curated-surfaces\")` and `GET /api/v1/endpoints` is wrapped in `csvListQuery(\"endpoints\")` (`src/contracts.mjs:1629-1658`), so `?format=csv` on either route returns a CSV today \u2014 the gap is purely front-end wiring.\n\n## Requirement\nAdd a Download CSV control to the Surfaces page and the Endpoints page's callable-endpoints table, each triggering a browser download of `?format=csv` against its own route with the view's current filters applied.\n\n## Deliverable\n- **Blocked on #3402** (\"FE: add a reusable `DownloadCsvButton` component\") \u2014 that component does not exist yet anywhere in `apps/ui/src` (confirmed via repo-wide search) and its issue is still open; the PR that would have shipped it, #3560, was **closed without merging**. This PR must consume whatever `DownloadCsvButton` (and any `buildCsvDownloadUrl`/URL-building helper it exports) #3402 ships \u2014 do not hand-roll a second CSV-trigger implementation.\n- `apps/ui/src/routes/surfaces.tsx`:\n  - Anchor: `SurfacesPage`'s `PageHero actions` block (lines 79-95), which already holds `TimeRangeScrub`, `ViewModeToggle`, `ResetFiltersButton`, `ShareButton` in that order.\n  - Add `DownloadCsvButton` to that actions group, wired to `/api/v1/surfaces` with the same filter params `SurfacesTable` builds as `baseParams` (lines 118-125: `q`, `sort`, `order`, `kind`, `provider`) so the exported CSV matches what's currently on screen.\n- `apps/ui/src/routes/endpoints.tsx`:\n  - Anchor: the sticky toolbar inside `EndpointsTable` (lines 573-670), which already renders `Search`, `Netuid`, `Provider`, `Region`, `Health`, `Eligibility`, `Reset filters`, `Callable only`, `ViewModeToggle`.\n  - Add `DownloadCsvButton` to that toolbar, wired to `/api/v1/endpoints`.\n  - Note the asymmetry with surfaces: `EndpointsTable` calls `endpointsQuery()` with **no server params** (line 351) \u2014 every filter (`category`, `provider`, `health`, `region`, `eligibility`, `netuid`, `callable`, `q`) is applied client-side over the full fetched set (lines 472-497). Decide and document in the PR whether the CSV button exports the full unfiltered `/api/v1/endpoints` set or maps the active client-side filters onto matching query params for the export request \u2014 pick one and be consistent, don't silently export something different from what the visible table shows without a note in the PR body.\n- \"Done\" = clicking the button on either page downloads a `.csv` file of that page's rows (respecting whichever filter behavior was chosen above), with no other visual or layout change to either page.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] `apps/ui/src/routes/surfaces.tsx` and `apps/ui/src/routes/endpoints.tsx` both appear in the diff, each importing and rendering `DownloadCsvButton` from the component #3402 ships\n- [ ] No new bespoke CSV-download implementation is added in either file \u2014 both call the shared component/helper, not `fetch`/`window.location` ad hoc\n- [ ] Surfaces' button targets `/api/v1/surfaces` and reflects the page's active `q`/`sort`/`order`/`kind`/`provider` filters in the export\n- [ ] Endpoints' button targets `/api/v1/endpoints`, and the PR description states explicitly whether the export is filtered or full-set (matching whichever behavior was implemented)\n- [ ] Neither page's existing table markup, columns, or unrelated controls (filters, sort headers, pagination, view toggle) change\n- [ ] `npm run lint`, `npm run format:check`, and `apps/ui` tests pass\n- [ ] Before/after screenshots included for both `/surfaces` and `/endpoints` per the repo's UI-PR requirement\n\n## Non-goals\n- Do not implement `DownloadCsvButton` itself in this PR \u2014 that is #3402's deliverable; this issue only consumes it\n- Do not touch the other CSV-wiring siblings in this batch (#3403 Subnets, #3404 Blocks, #3406 Extrinsics, #3407 Accounts, #3409 subnet-detail neuron table) \u2014 each is its own PR\n- No backend changes \u2014 `csvListQuery(\"curated-surfaces\")` and `csvListQuery(\"endpoints\")` already exist and are untouched by this issue\n- Do not add a netuid filter or any other new filter control to either page (that's tracked separately, e.g. #3421 for Surfaces) \u2014 this issue is CSV export only\n\n## Size\nSize: S \u2014 keep this PR small (aim for \u226410 files / \u22641000 LOC).\n\nPart of #2542.",
